{
  "example": "`fn[load]` moves unchanged from `src/config.rs` to `src/config/load.rs`, and\nnothing else changes. `habeas refactor --map 'src/config.rs#fn[load]=src/config/load.rs#fn[load]'`\nrewrites the outline inputs that read it, recomputes the reference-set digests\nof the requirements it implements, rewrites `` `src/config.rs#fn[load]` `` in\ntheir rationales, and validation then passes without calling a model.\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.outline_inputs`\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.reference_digest`\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.rationale.addresses`\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.equivalence`",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.refactor.moved_function` describes a concrete case. `fn[load]` moves unchanged from `src/config.rs` to `src/config/load.rs`, and `habeas refactor --map 'src/config.rs#fn[load]=src/config/load.rs#fn[load]'` is run. The expected outcomes are that outline inputs are rewritten, reference-set digests are recomputed, rationale addresses are rewritten, and validation passes without a model.\n\n`tests/refactor.rs#fn[a_moved_function_keeps_its_evidence_current]` carries the `{test}` reference. It covers the scenario and each outcome:\n\n- **Setup.** The `project` helper builds a fixture. `author` writes current evidence for `rules.load` and `rules.check`, using real outline inputs and the real reference-set digest. The test asserts that validation is clean with `errors(root)` before the move.\n- **The move.** `move_load` moves the unchanged `load` into `src/config/load.rs`, with an empty `extra` so the function body is identical. The test asserts that validation then reports a stale error mentioning `fn[load]`. That shows the refactor is what fixes it.\n- **Command run.** The test runs the exact `--map` mapping from the example and asserts that the command succeeds.\n- **Outline inputs rewritten.** It asserts that `record[\"inputs\"][1][\"file\"]` is `src/config/load.rs`. The other outline input, `fn[verify]`, stays in `src/config.rs`.\n- **Reference digest recomputed.** The `references` digest changes because the `{impl}` site moves files. The test asserts `errors(root)` is empty after the refactor. That validation compares the stored digest against the current reference set, so a wrong or missing digest would fail it.\n- **Rationale rewritten.** It asserts the exact new rationale. `` `src/config.rs#fn[load]` `` becomes `` `src/config/load.rs#fn[load]` ``. The `rules.load` code span and the `src/config.rs` mention for `verify` are untouched.\n- **Validation passes without a model.** After the refactor, `errors(root)` is empty. The test runs the plain CLI and the validation library, with no model supplied. The stale state before the refactor shows the pass comes from the rewrite.\n- **Nothing else changes.** The `snapshot` comparison of every other file passes. The `rules.check` record is byte-identical and is absent from the report. The report shows `Changed 1 records:\\n- evidence/rules.load.json`.\n- **Idempotence.** A second run reports `Changed 0 records:`.\n\nThe example's cited requirements (`outline_inputs`, `reference_digest`, `rationale.addresses`, `equivalence`) are applied in this case. Each rewrite is gated on the mapped-back state matching. The test does so with unchanged content, and its post-refactor validation passes just as it did before the move. I found no gap.",
  "references": "8832d7de8f757b1eab512f27090a43f6e073ba7aba1a2379baa5bf15ce0495d3",
